# Domain Finder

Tools live in `tools/domain-finder-skill/`. Adjust the paths below if you
cloned it somewhere else.

## Check availability

```bash
python3 tools/domain-finder-skill/scripts/check-domains.py --tlds com,ai,io \
  snapkit vaultly forgely --available-only
```

Output includes first-year **and renewal** price. The renewal column matters:
`.xyz` costs $2.04 the first year and $12.98 every year after.

Useful flags: `--available-only`, `--max-price 20`, `--json`, `--no-cache`,
`--plan` (preview request cost without spending it).

## Generate candidates

```bash
python3 tools/domain-finder-skill/scripts/gen-names.py \
  --roots snap,clip,vault --suffixes ify,ly,kit --max-len 6 \
  | python3 tools/domain-finder-skill/scripts/check-domains.py \
      --tlds com --available-only
```

Patterns: `root+suffix`, `prefix+root`, `prefix+root+suffix`, `root+root`,
`blend`.

## Rules

- **Pass the whole candidate list in one call.** One call with 60 domains costs
  3 requests; 60 single-domain calls cost 60 and will get throttled. Never loop
  the script over a list.
- **Never guess availability.** If the tool is not configured, say so and point
  at `tools/domain-finder-skill/references/environment.md`. Do not answer from
  memory or from a web search.
- **Never present an unresolved lookup as available.** `lookup failed`,
  `unknown`, and `no RDAP for this TLD` are all "don't know", not "yes". The
  script exits `3` when anything is unresolved.
- **Check brand collisions** before recommending a name. An available domain
  that collides with an established product is an SEO fight the user did not
  choose.
- **Read-only.** This never buys, transfers, or changes DNS. Purchases happen at
  the user's registrar.

Full workflow: `tools/domain-finder-skill/AGENTS.md`
